popcorn source code is released under the MIT License, see LICENSE. This
repository contains no third-party source code. The prebuilt test firmware
under tests/firmware/periph/prebuilt and the prebuilt example firmware under
examples/*/*/prebuilt contain object code compiled from the firmware-only
packages listed last. Unicorn and reflex are git
submodules under third_party/, pinned by commit. The other components below
are downloaded at build time from their upstream archives, pinned by version
and verified by sha256. Everything is compiled on the user's machine. The built
Python extension links Unicorn statically, so an installed popcorn extension is
a combined work subject to GPL-2.0-only.

Unicorn CPU emulator, popcorn fork at commit
c388e255f7418e1f1402cb3b35fce663be08fcbb, submodule third_party/unicorn
  https://github.com/Garcia6l20/unicorn, branch popcorn
  Upstream: https://github.com/unicorn-engine/unicorn, commit
  938efd13aeab73155f31cf707a2094c6ccaa36dd, modified as follows.
  2026-09-25, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c: host reads and writes of the M-profile
    special registers MSP, PSP, PRIMASK, BASEPRI, BASEPRI_MAX and FAULTMASK,
    and host writes of CONTROL, work in any mode. Upstream reads them as zero
    and ignores writes when the core is in unprivileged Thread mode.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added test_arm_m_unprivileged_special_regs.
  2026-09-26, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - include/unicorn/arm.h, qemu/target/arm/unicorn_arm.c: added
    UC_ARM_REG_MSPLIM and UC_ARM_REG_PSPLIM, host access to the ARMv8-M
    stack limit registers of the current security state. Upstream has no
    register id for them.
  - bindings/: regenerated the ARM constant files of the dotnet, go, java,
    pascal, python, ruby and zig bindings with the two new register ids.
  - tests/unit/test_arm.c: added test_arm_v8m_stack_limit_regs.
  2026-10-01, Sylvain Garcia <garcia.6l20@gmail.com>:
  - include/unicorn/unicorn.h, include/uc_priv.h, uc.c,
    qemu/accel/tcg/cputlb.c: added UC_CTL_UC_DROP_STORE and
    uc_ctl_drop_store(), which a UC_HOOK_MEM_WRITE_PROT callback returning
    true calls to discard the store and continue. Upstream either commits
    the store into the read-only memory or discards it, depending on how the
    region was mapped and written.
  - bindings/: regenerated the unicorn_const files of the dotnet, go, java,
    pascal, python, ruby and zig bindings with the new control id.
  - tests/unit/test_mem.c: added test_mem_write_prot_drop_store,
    test_mem_write_prot_handled_commits and
    test_mem_write_prot_drop_store_scope.
